description:
**TITLE:** Management Information Specialist

**SALARY:** Accepting bids, No Benefits

**LOCATION:** San Pablo

**REPORTS TO:** Executive Director

**STATUS:** CONTRACT

The Management Information Specialist is responsible for maintaining and troubleshooting computer systems, supporting staff on individual computer and network use, knowledge of phone systems, installing and maintaining hardware and software, and managing the network.

ESSENTIAL DUTIES

Manage network;

Maintain and troubleshoot agency computer systems;

Support staff on software, the network, email system and databases;

Install and maintain hardware and software;

Perform regular backups of the computer network.

REQUIREMENTS

· Bachelor's degree or three years experience in PC systems administration;

* Two years experience in administering Microsoft Word, Excel, Access and Outlook;
* Administration experience with Windows Server 2003 \\+;

· Proven ability to solve problems and work well with other staff members;

· Proven ability to work well independently;

· Ability to attain and maintain DOJ background clearance;

· Communicate technical knowledge to non\\-technical users.

To apply, send a letter of interest and resume or proposal to Community Violence Solutions at admin@cvsolutions.org.

COMMUNITY VIOLENCE SOLUTIONS is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on account of race, cultural or religious background, disability, or sexual preference. All qualified candidates of all backgrounds are encouraged to apply.

Job Type: Contract

Pay: $25\\.00 \\- $30\\.00 per hour

Expected hours: 10 per week

Experience:

* Customer service: 1 year (Preferred)

Ability to Commute:

* San Pablo, CA 94806 (Required)

Ability to Relocate:

* San Pablo, CA 94806: Relocate before starting work (Required)

Work Location: In person

**About Socomec Inc.**  
Socomec (the “Company”) was founded in 1922 and has its global headquarters in France. Socomec designs and manufactures cutting\\-edge products and solutions within its core areas of expertise: Critical Power, Power Control \\& Safety, Energy Efficiency, and Energy Storage. With 10% of its annual sales revenue being reinvested into research and development, Socomec even has its very own state\\-of\\-the\\-art testing laboratories.

As an independent manufacturer, with 12 international manufacturing sites, Socomec is known for its innovative, high\\-quality products. We have grown to a global team of over 3,600 employees. Socomec is comprised of 28 subsidiary companies worldwide, with a strong and growing presence in North America.

**About This Role:**

The Field Engineering Services Division provides professional field services and technical support for the full range of Powersmiths and Socomec products. These services are delivered to a wide range of customers in power distribution, critical power markets, green and brown field buildings, and data centers. These market spaces are growing and are forecasted to grow substantially on a global scale. Powersmiths and Socomec have developed products and services specifically to serve these growing markets.

Field Service Technicians are responsible for the performance of professional and technical services at our client sites that may include transformer surveys and baseline measurements, system startup, commissioning, integrated system testing, preventive and planned maintenance, emergency repairs, etc. These services are performed on Powersmiths and Socomec products that include Low\\-Voltage Transformers, Power Distribution Units (PDU), Static Transfer Switches (STS), Uninterruptible Power Supplies (UPS), Energy Storage Systems (ESS), and other devices and accessories.

**Key Responsibilities and Accountabilities:**

General Duties:

* Maintain excellence in safety ensuring that all work is performed in a safe and professional manner;
* Communicate, coordinate, and manage a complex schedule including arranging for travel and site access to highly secure environments (Military \\& Government facilities, sensitive banking, or other secure data centers, etc.).
* Responsible for the accurate and timely performance of on\\-site activities and delivery of reports on time;
* Work closely with client engineers, contractors, and other contacts to meet project requirements and ensure customer satisfaction;
* Review and interpret work instructions, installation manuals, commissioning schedules and scripts, maintenance manuals, electrical drawings and one\\-line diagrams in order to accurately and safely execute work;
* Coordinate with technical support and management teams to ensure timely escalation of issues;
* Maintain a learning mindset to continuously improve knowledge and abilities needed to support Powersmiths and Socomec products and services.

Field Service Technician duties:

*Field Service Technician I* is an entry level position focused on skill building for successful progression to higher levels. Key duties of a Technician include:

* Meet general duties above while under the supervision of senior technicians/mentors;
* Learn and continuously apply safety policies and procedures to ensure safe completion of all activities;
* Develop a thorough understanding of site transformer surveys, transformer measurement and verification, and energy savings calculations;
* Learn how to identify and analyze constraints and onsite transformer configurations to assist in the design, configuration, and production of replacement transformers;
* Prepare and submit site reports on a timely basis;
* Complete classroom and field training for start\\-up, commissioning, preventive maintenance and basic troubleshooting of PDUs and small/medium UPS systems.

**Essential Qualifications, Knowledge and Skills:**

* Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering or related discipline preferred or equivalent electrical or power electronics field experience or related military experience;
* Strong understanding of, or willingness to learn and adhere to, health and safety regulations and protocols including OSHA 1910 and NFPA 70E;
* Knowledge of, or willingness to learn, electrical code, transformers, power electronics, PDU, UPS, energy storage systems (ESS), and static transfer switches (STS);
* Demonstrated ability to deliver the highest level of customer service while working independently;
* Demonstrated ability to plan travel, develop and execute complex scheduling of client site visits;
* Strong knowledge of, or willingness to learn, the energy conservation market;
* Ability to collect and synthesize information from multiple sources in order to execute a large and diverse number of projects, tasks and issues with professionalism and persistence;
* Able to effectively represent Powersmiths and effectively communicate with clients, contractors, commissioning agents, and others at varying technical levels;
* Ability to adhere to standards and ensure compliance with customers’ specific requirements on each project;
* Capable of working in a fast\\-paced entrepreneurial environment, managing and accurately completing multiple tasks within tight deadlines and in accordance with the project deliverables and customer requirements;
* Able to obtain clearance to access schools and government installations; background checks and fingerprinting are required by customers on some projects;
* Must be able to purchase airline tickets, rent vehicles, reserve lodging at own expense with full reimbursement on a monthly basis.

**Working Conditions:**

* Field work (in electrical rooms, mechanical rooms, data centers, etc.) and home office or office environment;
* Extensive travel nation\\-wide; occasional international travel (Canada, Europe, Asia, etc.);
* Home based office.

**Employment Requirements:**

* Successful completion of a pre\\-employment drug test and background check. In addition, since this is a safety\\-sensitive role, ongoing or periodic drug testing and background checks may be required throughout employment in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws.
* Commitment to Health and Safety best practice and regulations
* Adherence to company policies
* Computer skills, including Microsoft Excel and basic TCP/IP networking
* Valid drivers license
* Valid passport for international travel

**Work Authorization :**

* Must be legally authorized to work in the United States without company sponsorship

**Physical Demands :**

* Mobility: Ability to move about in various environments, including customer sites, manufacturing facilities, and office settings. This may involve standing, walking, climbing, bending, or kneeling for extended periods.
* Stationary Work: Ability to remain in a stationary position, whether seated or standing, for prolonged periods when completing tasks such as diagnostics, repairs, or documentation.
* Manual Dexterity: Repeating motions that may include the wrists, hands, and/or fingers for tasks such as wiring, equipment assembly, and tool handling.
* Lifting and Carrying: Ability to lift, carry, or move items weighing up to 50 pounds on an occasional basis.
* Visual and Auditory Requirements: Ability to read technical documents, diagrams, and computer screens, and to communicate effectively with customers and team members.
* Travel: Regular travel to customer sites is required, which may involve driving or other modes of transportation.

**Compensation:**

* Position is salaried non\\-exempt.
* Socomec offers an interesting, innovative work environment, and a competitive benefits package.​
* Note that approved business expenses (travel, accommodation, etc.) are reimbursed through the company’s expense reporting system

Upon request, we will provide reasonable accommodation for disabilities to support participation of candidates in all aspects of the recruitment process. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment *without regard to race, color, religion, sex or national origin*.

We thank all those who apply. However, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.

Job Type: Full\\-time

Pay: $75,000\\.00 \\- $80,000\\.00 per year

Benefits:

* 401(k)

Application Question(s):

* What is your expected salary range? (a specific range would help us to have an idea)
* Do you have experience with 3 phase 480VAC and Power Electronics?
* Are you comfortable with the 75% travel required for this job?
* Would you be able to visit customers sites across Los Angeles, CA area on regular basis?

Work Location: On the road

